# Backend Rules - NestJS + Prisma 7 + PostgreSQL

## NestJS Architecture
- **Module-first** - each feature has its own module
- **Dependency injection** - use constructor injection
- **Repository pattern** with Prisma - thin controllers, fat services
- **DTOs for everything** - no plain objects in/out
- **Pipes for validation** - class-validator + class-transformer
- **Guards for auth** - reusable, composable
- **Interceptors for cross-cutting** - logging, transformation, caching
- **Custom decorators** for repeated logic
- **Global exception filter** - consistent error responses

## File Structure
```
src/
  ├── common/           # Reusable pipes, guards, interceptors, filters
  │   ├── decorators/
  │   ├── filters/
  │   ├── guards/
  │   ├── interceptors/
  │   └── pipes/
  ├── config/           # Configuration files
  ├── health/           # Health check module
  ├── prisma/           # Prisma service + module
  │   └── prisma.service.ts
  ├── {feature}/        # Feature modules
  │   ├── dto/
  │   │   ├── create-{entity}.dto.ts
  │   │   ├── update-{entity}.dto.ts
  │   │   └── query-{entity}.dto.ts
  │   ├── entities/
  │   ├── {feature}.controller.ts
  │   ├── {feature}.service.ts
  │   ├── {feature}.module.ts
  │   └── {feature}.service.spec.ts
  ├── app.module.ts
  └── main.ts
```

## Prisma 7 Best Practices
- **Driver adapter required** - use @prisma/adapter-pg with pg Pool
- **Never use url in schema** - datasource block has provider only
- **Prisma config file** - url goes in prisma.config.ts
- **PrismaService** - singleton managing connection lifecycle
- **Transaction boundaries** - wrap related operations
- **Select specific fields** - avoid `select: true`
- **Pagination always** - cursor or offset with max limits
- **Soft delete pattern** - deletedAt field, filter in queries
- **Migrations versioned** - never edit migration after apply
- **Seed data** - idempotent seed script

## API Design
- **RESTful principles** - nouns as resources, verbs as HTTP methods
- **Versioning** - /api/v1/ prefix
- **Consistent response format**:
  ```typescript
  { data: T, meta?: PaginationMeta, message?: string }
  ```
- **HTTP status codes** correctly:
  - 200: OK, 201: Created, 204: No Content
  - 400: Bad Request, 401: Unauthorized, 403: Forbidden, 404: Not Found
  - 409: Conflict, 422: Unprocessable Entity, 500: Server Error
- **Query params** for filtering, sorting, pagination
- **Route params** for resource identification only
- **Swagger decorators** on all DTOs and controllers

## Database Access
- **PrismaService** via DI - never instantiate PrismaClient directly
- **Repository abstraction** - service layer uses Prisma, not controller
- **Transaction scope** - wrap related writes
- **N+1 prevention** - use include/select wisely
- **Indexing strategy** - index foreign keys, query fields
- **Raw queries** only when necessary - prefer Prisma Client

## Validation & DTOs
- **class-validator decorators** on all DTO properties
- **Validation pipes** at controller level
- **Type coercion** via class-transformer
- **Custom validators** for business rules
- **Swagger integration** - @ApiProperty with examples
- **Read-only DTOs** - use `readonly` keyword
- **Partial types** - use mapped types for updates

## Testing Strategy
- **Unit tests** for services (mock Prisma)
- **Integration tests** for controllers (supertest)
- **E2E tests** for critical flows
- **Prisma mocking** - mock PrismaService, not PrismaClient directly
- **Factory pattern** for test data - use @faker-js/faker
- **Arrange-Act-Assert** structure
- **One describe per method**, one it per scenario

## Error Handling
- **Domain exceptions** - extend HttpException
- **Global exception filter** - logs + consistent response format
- **Prisma error mapping** - P2002 = 409 Conflict, P2025 = 404
- **Never leak stack traces** in production
- **Structured logging** - use NestJS Logger

## Async Patterns
- **async/await** exclusively - no raw promises
- **Promise.all** for independent operations
- **Sequential** for dependent operations
- **Never floating promises** - always await or handle
- **Timeout handling** for external calls

## Security Backend
- **Helmet** for security headers
- **CORS** configured for specific origins only
- **Rate limiting** - per user/IP
- **JWT strategy** - Passport.js
- **Password hashing** - bcrypt, never store plain
- **Input sanitization** - class-validator
- **SQL injection** - impossible with Prisma, but validate for raw queries
